  problem:{title:"The Afternoon Alone",
    text:["Mariam, 13, is looking after her little brother Zayed, aged 4, while her mother is at the shop. She leaves a pan of oil on the stove and goes to answer her phone.","Zayed climbs on a chair to reach the medicine cupboard. Minutes later, Mariam smells smoke coming from the kitchen."],
    qs:[["Identify the hazards described in the text.","Unattended hot oil, a child climbing, and medicines he can reach."],
        ["What could the consequences be for Mariam and Zayed?","Fire, burns, a fall or poisoning: serious injury or worse."],
        ["What should Mariam do now, step by step?","Get Zayed away, turn off the heat if safe, get out and call 997. Never throw water on an oil fire."],
        ["Which safety rules were ignored? How could the accidents be prevented?","Supervise young children, never leave cooking, keep medicines locked away."]]},
