  problem:{title:"The Museum Choice",
    text:["A new museum in Dubai has space for only ONE Chinese invention in its main hall. Salem wants the compass, because it links to Arab sailors like Ahmad ibn Majid.","Aisha wants paper, because without it there would be no books or libraries. Their teacher asks them to agree and explain their choice."],
    qs:[["Identify the problem Salem and Aisha face.","They must choose one invention and justify their choice."],
        ["What is the impact of each invention on the world and on the UAE?","Compass: travel and trade by sea. Paper: books, learning and records."],
        ["Suggest a fair way for them to decide, and give your choice.","List criteria (impact, UAE link), compare, then decide with reasons."],
        ["Which inventions changed learning and travel? How are they linked?","Paper and printing spread ideas; the compass spread trade, and ideas travelled with it."]]},
  create:{title:"Inventions That Changed the World",
    options:[["Museum label","Write a museum label for one Chinese invention: what it is, who made it, when, and why it matters."],["Speech","Write a one-minute speech persuading the class that one invention is the most important."],["Infographic","Create an infographic showing how one invention travelled from China to the Arab world."]],
    must:["One invention","A date or inventor","An Arab or UAE link","A catchy title"]},
